# Close the window, and the agents keep working, for the site's box beside
# "Each agent runs in tmux" (site/how-it-works.html) and a social reel.
# Three agents are at work; one is shown. The window closes, which quits
# the app, and opens again with nothing of the old one: the cards come back
# where they were, still working, and the shown agent's terminal has moved
# on meanwhile.
# Film it with docs/demo/record.sh, then cut it with docs/demo/cut.sh;
# the steps are in docs/demo/README.md.
#
# A window's first terminal can hold its drawing up for some seconds on a
# busy Mac, so each Show is followed by two Sleeps: the first ends when the
# window draws again, and the second is seen. The window that opens again
# takes as long to connect and draw its terminal. The cuts keep two seconds
# of the closed window, then jump to the window as it opens and connects,
# and over the empty list it shows until the core's sessions are in. The
# jumps are timed for the film of 8 November 2026; check them against the
# frames after filming again.
#
# The phone cut stays on the cards: they go, the window's place is empty
# while it is closed, and they come back where they were, still working.
# cut: jump close+2 open+1.8
# cut: jump open+2.45 opened-0.25
# cut: site close-4 end opened+1
# cut: phone close-3 end
# cut: shot close-3 540 0 0
# cut: caption close-0.9 open+1.85 top Close the window. They keep working.
# cut: caption opened-0.2 end top Open it again: nothing stopped.
# cut: readme close-2 opened+2
# cut: sheet close-1.5 close+1.2 opened+0.4 opened+3 down+1.5
Set Size 1024x640
Set Appearance light
Set Palette evergreen
Set Backdrop E9EBDF

Spawn @acme-api document the orders api
Spawn @acme-web speed up the product page
Spawn @acme-billing add receipts to the invoices

Sleep 500ms
Show 2
Sleep 1s
Sleep 5s
Close
Sleep 3.5s
Open
Sleep 1s
Sleep 4s
Down
Sleep 3.5s
